                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 351.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum left by Mr. Jackson with Baron von der
                        Taun, Bavarian chargé d’affaires August 30, 1895</hi>.</head>
                <p>The embassy of the United States is informed by its Government that Mr. Louis
                    Stern, of New York, sailed on board the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Majestic</hi>, of, the White Star Line, with his wife, four children, two
                    maids, governess, and tutor, on February 27 last, and that the person of the
                    same name who sailed in the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> from
                    New York on May 9 for Hamburg was a Mr. Louis Stern, of New Orleans, in whose
                    family was included a boy under 12 years of age.</p>
            </div>
